# One regex per line. Links matching any line are skipped by lychee.
# Keep this short and explain every entry; an ignored link is a link nobody checks.
# Example: a vendor portal that blocks bots
# ^https://portal\.example-vendor\.com/
# Placeholder hosts and RFC 5737 documentation addresses in the examples and the
# range's Nexus mirror (192.0.2.2 stands in for the operator's).
^https?://server:
^https?://192\.0\.2\.
^https?://198\.51\.100\.
^https?://203\.0\.113\.
^https?://github\.com/CHANGE-ME/
# cyber.gov.au answers lychee with an HTTP/2 protocol error although the page
# exists; the ACSC event-logging reference stays linked for readers.
^https://www\.cyber\.gov\.au/
